<SubSection title="What is Human Centered Design?" id="What is Human Centered Design?">
<p>Human Centered Design (HCD) is the process by which engineers and designers put humans at the center of the design process through needs finding and iterative design to provide solutions that are useful to stakeholders. HCD is a problem-solving approach that uses design thinking methods and tools to identify the unmet needs of a population in order to collaboratively and iteratively develop solutions.</p>
</SubSection>
